{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuivgvQr7XgvYCX8QexT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As far as I know, the Vitest CLI has no flag that repeats every test (`--retry` only re-runs tests that fail, which hides flakiness instead of finding it). Repeating is set per test with the `repeats` option, e.g. `test('my test', { repeats: 10 }, () => { ... })` or `describe('suite', { repeats: 10 }, ...)`. The test runs that many extra times and fails if any run fails.\n\nTo repeat the whole suite from the command line, loop over `vitest run`. In PowerShell: `1..20 | % { npx vitest run; if ($LASTEXITCODE) { break } }`. In bash: `for i in $(seq 20); do npx vitest run || break; done`. Add `--sequence.shuffle` to randomize test order and catch tests that depend on each other.\n\nI haven't checked this against the current docs, so run `npx vitest --help` to see whether your version has added a repeat flag."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5814,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5814},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b352cdb6-a358-41ed-9f3c-54b152a8f9c6","uuid":"6a62847b-ade6-46df-9b21-1c0fd96c1e95","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:16:14.176Z","request_id":"req_011Cfuivga5nGZxjnPvapffG"}
